25 1113 #uuid "5fcd2373-835d-58c0-a150-1972239e0d50" 13194139534648 true] [17592186301325 1145 "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{-1}^{a}{e}^{-2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x-1}]}_{-1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-1}}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{e}^{-2x}]}_{-1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2e}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{2a}}-{e}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\frac{1}{{e}^{2x}},$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{2x}}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{2x}}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/0064a1c234adc9cf5d28d16696bef8a72384a8cc9f85ecc865c5d4ba36dc0d49.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{2e}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{2a}}-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2e}(0-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534648 true] [17592186301326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301327 13194139534648 true] [17592186301326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301328 13194139534648 true] [17592186301326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301329 13194139534648 true] [17592186301326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301330 13194139534648 true] [17592186301326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301331 13194139534648 true] [17592186301326 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534648 true] [17592186301326 1041 "selection" 13194139534648 true] [17592186301326 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301330 13194139534648 true] [17592186301326 1110 #uuid "b5ab81b5-3047-554d-a157-6cbf4f7f74b1" 13194139534648 true] [17592